{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>These are the names, etc. The anointed, etc.</b> It returned to say <b>these are the names</b> a second time, and was not satisfied with what it said the first time — ״אֵלֶּה שְׁמוֹת״ etc. — and to finish by saying <b>the anointed</b> etc. It intended to restrict, so that none were anointed but these. Therefore it was precise in saying <b>these</b> to exclude all others. And from the first verse this was not heard to be the case, since it said ״וְאֵלֶּה״ — which would not be heard to exclude the children of Israel who preceded them. Understand this."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:05:53.758614194Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}